{"parentUuid":"a14c5d9d-c4ac-4f9b-a71e-c1361b27c7bc","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"9af44ced-bc96-4c0c-851c-b7a4d67027a3","agentId":"a26fb63d519ffd330","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ruuut2PQoZMAZoBWHjZ3fU","type":"tool_result","content":"173:## Resume a non-interactive session\n175:If you need to continue a previous run (for example, a two-stage pipeline), use the `resume` subcommand:\n179:codex exec resume --last \"fix the race conditions you found\"\n182:You can also target a specific session ID with `codex exec resume <SESSION_ID>`.\n1:# Non-interactive mode\n10:## When to use `codex exec`\n19:## Basic usage\n51:## Permissions and safety\n66:## Make output machine-readable\n90:## Create structured outputs with a schema\n129:## Authenticate in automation\n133:### Use API key auth\n173:## Resume a non-interactive session\n184:## Git repository required\n188:## Common automation patterns\n190:### Example: Autofix CI failures in GitHub Actions\n321:## Advanced stdin piping\n325:### Use prompt-plus-stdin\n337:### Summarize logs\n345:### Inspect TLS or HTTP issues\n353:### Prepare a Slack-ready update\n361:### Draft a pull request comment from CI logs\n371:### Use `codex exec -` when stdin is the prompt","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"c2dfc0c4-43df-49d8-91b3-f6bdd4b95df8","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:56:20.290Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a14c5d9d-c4ac-4f9b-a71e-c1361b27c7bc","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a26fb63d519ffd330","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a513ce3b392834fe0"}
