{"parentUuid":"56893aa7-e84d-41bd-bc42-d1475a69fc1d","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a26fb63d519ffd330","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CffXHagzobWLkr31TiduZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The sr-checks run is still going in the background; I'm waiting on its completion notice before pushing or opening a PR.\n\nStatus so far:\n- **codex x session-resume-unknown:** recorded, supported with two deviations. The real `codex exec resume <unknown>` exits 1 with a no-rollout message on stderr. It fires no hook at all (the statement's end-of-session hook included), so that is declared as a `capability-grounding` deviation. Only the unknown-session failure is modeled, declared as `modeled-surface`.\n- **cursor x session-resume-unknown:** recorded, unsupported. The real `cursor-agent --resume <unknown>` accepts the id, runs a new session under it and exits 0.\n- **Verification:** `go build`, `go vet`, gofmt and the tests I ran all pass. I did not run `internal/...` or `tools/...` after the rebase, and sr-checks is still pending.\n- **Not done yet:** push, PR and merge.\n\nChanges:\n- **Cells:** both cells are filled in `spec/capabilities/session-resume-unknown.yaml`.\n- **Runs:** new runs named `session-resume-unknown` under `codex-mock/snapshots/runs/` and `cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/`.\n- **Core:** `internal/session/resume.go` gains `ResumeAt`, which takes the hook phases that still fire as a parameter. `Resume` calls it with the end phase, so Claude's behaviour is unchanged.\n- **Adapter:** `codex-mock` now accepts `exec resume <id>` and fails an unknown id as recorded. It carries the `sr:provides` marker.\n- **Test:** `codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/resume_unknown_test.go`, with the `sr:proves` marker, replays the recorded run.\n- **Module map:** `internal/session/module.yaml` home list includes the new runner file.\n- **Script fix:** `codex-mock/snapshots/capture.sh` aborted silently when a run left no rollout (a failed