{"parentUuid":"c1f7f369-3644-4cac-8f31-83d1f9a7fe7e","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a26fb63d519ffd330","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cffard9MXDRdYbSvjM6oV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both pending cells for `session-resume-unknown` are resolved, and PR #103 is merged with all CI checks green. The first merge attempt failed because main had moved, so I rebased, re-ran sr-checks (clean) and merged on the new head.\n\n- **codex: supported, with one deviation.** The real `codex exec resume <unknown id>` exits 1 with a no-rollout message on stderr. It fires no hook at all, so the statement's end-of-session hook does not fire. That gap is declared as a `capability-grounding` deviation.\n- **cursor: unsupported.** The real `cursor-agent --resume <unknown id>` does not fail. It starts a new session under that id and exits 0. The cell cites the recorded run.\n- **Runs captured:** `session-resume-unknown` under both `codex-mock/snapshots/runs/` and `cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/`, one sample each.\n- **Mock:** `codex-mock` now accepts `exec resume <id>` and fails an unknown id as recorded. Resuming an existing session is not modeled, and I did not declare that as a deviation because the `modeled-surface` ADR does not cover it. The core `ResumeAt` in `internal/session/resume.go` takes the hook phases that still fire as a parameter, and Claude's behaviour is unchanged.\n- **Test:** `codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/resume_unknown_test.go` replays the recorded run.\n- **Capture script:** `codex-mock/snapshots/capture.sh` aborted silently when a run left no rollout, so I added `|| true` to its transcript loop.\n\nNothing is left red."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":199,"cache_read_input_tokens":136650,"output_tokens":553,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_